        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila succini Turing wavenumber at 2.8 µm (44 Ma, detail scale s0) (Drosophila succini)",
        "Drosophila succini Turing wavenumber at 2.8 µm (44 Ma, detail scale s0) faithfully reproduces Drosophila succini morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0.py, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3172_drosophila_succini_turing_wavelength_s0.lean implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila succini specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3172_drosophila_succini_turing_wavelength_s0.lean> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila succini" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A pixel identity between the spot field and an amber inclusion.",
        "does_not_claim: A signed nanopublication. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml was present.",
        "does_not_claim: That k_h (determinant minimizer) equals k_c above onset. Here k_h is about 7.30 and k_c is about 6.28.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Berryi lambda by scaling both diffusivities with (98.43/114)^2.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: D_u sweep from 0.25 to 3 times the succini value; lambda increases at every step.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Specimen mask: foreground fraction, circularity, coherency, and a Sobel-orientation KS distance.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Stem r = 8.40 and ablation r = 1 have negative sigma_max.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: sigma(k) from the Jacobian; k_c = argmax sigma; D_u chosen so lambda_c = 2.759e-06 m at r = 18.72.",
        "reported_in_source: Grimaldi 1987: amber Drosophilidae, including the Dominican record used as the 19 Ma successor context.",
        "reported_in_source: Hennig 1965: Drosophila succini, Baltic amber, Stuttgarter Beiträge zur Naturkunde 145.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the activator-substrate rate laws used here.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: reaction-diffusion selects a critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: Full-spectrum Pearson r of the PDE modes is about 0.79 because strongly damped modes mix the fast eigenvalue. The pre-registered band sigma > -0.25 has r > 0.98 and RMSE about 3e-5.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2.382 µm berryi wavelength is a scale transfer, not a fossil measurement.",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery card is not the holotype. CV similarity is to that card." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila succini (Eocene Baltic Amber Stem Drosophilid)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3172_drosophila_succini_turing_wavelength_s0.lean; output: docs/media/drosophila_succini_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila succini; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: reaction-diffusion selects a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: the activator-substrate rate laws used here. | Hennig 1965: Drosophila succini, Baltic amber, Stuttgarter Beiträge zur Naturkunde 145. | Grimaldi 1987: amber Drosophilidae, including the Dominican record used as the 19 Ma successor context.; reconstructed_in_script: sigma(k) from the Jacobian; k_c = argmax sigma; D_u chosen so lambda_c = 2.759e-06 m at r = 18.72. | D_u sweep from 0.25 to 3 times the succini value; lambda increases at every step. | Stem r = 8.40 and ablation r = 1 have negative sigma_max. | Berryi lambda by scaling both diffusivities with (98.43/114)^2. | Specimen mask: foreground fraction, circularity, coherency, and a Sobel-orientation KS distance.; transfer_boundary: The 2.382 µm berryi wavelength is a scale transfer, not a fossil measurement. | The gallery card is not the holotype. CV similarity is to that card. | Full-spectrum Pearson r of the PDE modes is about 0.79 because strongly damped modes mix the fast eigenvalue. The pre-registered band sigma > -0.25 has r > 0.98 and RMSE about 3e-5.; does_not_claim: A pixel identity between the spot field and an amber inclusion. | That k_h (determinant minimizer) equals k_c above onset. Here k_h is about 7.30 and k_c is about 6.28. | A signed nanopublication. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml was present.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
